# Not generated: only ak's first-review size count reads this mark (transitions.diff_lines), so
# the Go build lands one milestone at a time, free of that count's cap (`executor_lines`; owner
# rule, 20 Oct 2026), while every reviewer still reads every line of it.  GitHub collapses these
# diffs by default.
go/** linguist-generated
# Each milestone adds its own lines here: side by side they are both meant, never a conflict, so
# neighbouring claims neither park a run behind another (leases.py) nor stop a rebase at landing.
go/keys.txt merge=union
